WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
Quick cuts.

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:01.970
Football.

3
00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:02.910
Swimming.

4
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.000
Tennis.

5
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:08.420
And on the tennis court, a few of the
players are serving with their left hand.

6
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.640
Are left-handers more
likely to play tennis,

7
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.900
or does it just look that way?

8
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.880
A hunch isn't evidence.

9
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.960
How could you actually test it?

10
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.920
In this mission, you'll
set up a null hypothesis,

11
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.100
the no effect claim,
against an alternative:

12
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.170
what you're looking for evidence of.

13
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.620
You'll set out a contingency
table, a grid of counts,

14
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.030
and work out the frequencies
you'd expect with no link.

15
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.200
And you'll compare a p-value
with a significance level,

16
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.190
fixed before you test.

17
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.710
Your mission: work out how you could
test whether left-handers are more likely

18
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.840
to play tennis.
